{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0e4c68c55bc086e9e46ff6810ae365a3b7b08fb71cc454ad4734515ae4b16b4e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9defb9061f44f514d78e2b714f71dd2e4767f2622336754a7e9ee5a0a6f4deda"],"source_ids":["src_a1d4cc1b8c3b514fb295c028808325ee"],"text":"The execution mode is configured via the execution_service.kernel_mode parameter in taskweaver_config.json, with 'container' as the default value.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_314e8e526daeb73cac57a3faa2e35a795b9a57ae5ccf9b4ba7444e69ade76c96","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9a8d0e40a0ed21fefb633bdbaff7fd34121e16b02ddfd679b31b9efa39042328"],"source_ids":["src_a1d4cc1b8c3b514fb295c028808325ee"],"text":"Container mode has documented limitations: slower startup, limited host access with only the session workspace directory mounted (files must be uploaded via /upload or the web upload button), and packages must be added to the Dockerfile and image rebuilt.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_396041a641794214f945b7487fc15568d7f2fbaba9f8d8cb2414e95ec75585e1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5f41286d1582198648eea1f585812cf0a82c8af0d21915c73f82ef575cb7b5ca","slc_f1937ef781e14604fc43516e0833c3aeee9ea8571c1ffc2184aa82dd3e45b3b3","slc_fb7aa483b2ff549600e9ac906d375715199dab5bdc76b90b3cb427642ef71538"],"source_ids":["src_0c30b6d7b0005bf9a831c3290ce0af2a"],"text":"LLM configuration is provided in a taskweaver_config.json file, e.g. llm.api_key and llm.model for OpenAI, with other LLMs and advanced configurations supported per the docs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_40d8986fa5da28efbff70827ee87237f9817d18e424d619b5df06072ce1f0d6f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_85bd59c095192aca14987ae58e79d75ef4b3da7e62b398b0cc2a104822d57869"],"source_ids":["src_a2d788c97d10553dac4a814bfe21c334"],"text":"Shared information is stored as attachments inside posts rather than a separate structure so that, if a round fails, its shared entries can be filtered out by round status, analogous to transaction logging.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_57168a4273beb7921e705cb4291ec282b5d9e6f2c90ad6b8aed04951555fa87f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8ddad5ed2af2facd89251a884f01bd99c7c12798bde795b76acf9fea60aabed6"],"source_ids":["src_a2d788c97d10553dac4a814bfe21c334"],"text":"The fixed star-topology orchestration is acknowledged by the docs as a limitation, though it preserves role independence.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5ac28aad81a5ae6cfe17a91db831a4ac7d2ed9a3e3c3399ae4f4e0ff794fdd89","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2921d148ac2c730c1934c59630d2b4e29bf5a2c36b69007aaecf34b7aafcc0e8"],"source_ids":["src_0c30b6d7b0005bf9a831c3290ce0af2a"],"text":"TaskWeaver is described as a code-first agent framework for planning and executing data analytics tasks, interpreting user requests as code snippets and coordinating plugin functions in a stateful manner.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6060f9975e9a49c013a25c77253d1df82e520bbffe6a51cee50227af4cb264b1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8ddad5ed2af2facd89251a884f01bd99c7c12798bde795b76acf9fea60aabed6","slc_99813c89bd85ae9a0437b45a467f74c20e2d9a295310733ec2d2f53a6c08430d"],"source_ids":["src_a2d788c97d10553dac4a814bfe21c334"],"text":"Roles are orchestrated in a star topology with the Planner at the center: the User interacts only with the Planner, which plans and instructs peripheral roles, each of which knows only the Planner.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_60910a6d43a6c3bf0a3b78620a2f083192a2f3c9ab4ee2d91e81752d002e9516","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6040381e9b7c46ec68e877d33fd77affd6259151573f73efd8f0cd833748bd40"],"source_ids":["src_0c30b6d7b0005bf9a831c3290ce0af2a"],"text":"Unlike frameworks that track only chat history, TaskWeaver preserves both chat history and code execution history including in-memory data, which it says helps with complex data like high-dimensional tables.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_65617be7cc443092f16b715769d1c8ba4c472c67e2cc8a14e50d89c7ac331e0d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1823266ae891292f97ce90ad80b0c99afc4780b8896b5c8a6930074ac76b6933","slc_3d8477cf84f0553858f9b2a37f300c5a17c5d6686cfe471a392e4cd901d506ab","slc_7856fb1bbc451bddfa6f2836b5b9b4bdcb0cdeb327808c4b7fb353311a0d95ee"],"source_ids":["src_a2d788c97d10553dac4a814bfe21c334"],"text":"The memory module stores conversation history between the user and roles plus a shared memory of information purposefully shared between roles; implementation is in taskweaver/memory/memory.py.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8752994f192f36c00576c975dd0610ff2150b9bc7aa07a4e448be047b11596a7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2c2a1db006f738e917846952b8cfddae24a9b48ed24defa3e79665e3e0b05487","slc_9defb9061f44f514d78e2b714f71dd2e4767f2622336754a7e9ee5a0a6f4deda"],"source_ids":["src_a1d4cc1b8c3b514fb295c028808325ee"],"text":"Code execution supports 'local' and 'container' modes; container mode (the default) runs code in a Docker container for a more secure environment, while local mode runs code as a subprocess and could let malicious users or LLM-generated code harm the host.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_95887d86b45a2639936f150f85a3c2ec68c930febe311c533d8f4ef8eb820c9b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6d6a0936179e18dd40e6ed22cc0f75f4c49184a82a35a947f7b5f8ae646d40d3","slc_a7e8e91cb16fcb6ae66a176ff7367d25062e8e0f935e7dea6749b00e09fafd44"],"source_ids":["src_252cbbd8f1ef5a58b191a93308faeb03"],"text":"In the default flow, the user query goes to the Planner, which generates a plan for the CodeInterpreter; the interpreter executes and returns results, and the Planner summarizes them back, possibly iterating multiple times.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_96cf7bbea9574367a22df3f9f87ee918392a2122c8322c91ab82c8c990096f1f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d78c6ade3874a0e5b90502894843493cc5171725b88698b58f9094a2ce4dcb26"],"source_ids":["src_a1d4cc1b8c3b514fb295c028808325ee"],"text":"The default executor Docker image contains only dependencies from requirements.txt; users needing extra packages must modify the Dockerfile at TaskWeaver/docker/ces_container/Dockerfile and rebuild.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a571a048c660e12740a4e21bea33f2f7d58b575d9984f971272ff9a0f46a15e4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_774c405d348959a797e837d744e9c6ef52d43087be9a7932a3eafd1183b25cbf","slc_9a265c784c9c27466efc007a8ca25b7e67ee3aba482e30e100491418bc622f69"],"source_ids":["src_0c30b6d7b0005bf9a831c3290ce0af2a"],"text":"The project requires Python 3.10 or 3.11 per its README badge and states Python >= 3.10 is required for installation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b9791d56140c2af904f104fcfccc03828779718c0bfc688a94a359169c36da58","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a962b267e678f6080cd6324538283c47f2af646490e3e5e339509953a7c05b41"],"source_ids":["src_a1d4cc1b8c3b514fb295c028808325ee"],"text":"Generated code is executed via a Jupyter Kernel, chosen as a well-established interactive computing tool supporting many languages.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d85f192d45fff6877b53c81a35024e91c2e8c587342b861ab086c11abcf961ba","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3be333358fc83c183d3ff441739c699eb4ca265e96834a612027181c0bfb7413","slc_4fed85d251dafa5d9235dd3250c5a189fef8967d2b37a0fe87f3c8dfeb414ec1","slc_8a9a77d387d63610cf6a22eb2be842056d22b077a76003430617ba849fc3ae8c","slc_dfbdcdb190102abb7255f9e89f1fd4d16dbb10e5c444828c1b4b6626cf50ba93"],"source_ids":["src_a2d788c97d10553dac4a814bfe21c334"],"text":"Shared memory entries are attachments on posts with fields type, content, scope ('round' or 'conversation'), and id; round-scoped entries expire with the round, and later entries with the same type from a role overwrite earlier ones.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_de4997394b6bac68582e9ff37a7e6f7572b8560d37671d47cd46a1277cf262b5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"microsoft/taskweaver@d44ddef23f90 snapshot e3f1b857b4e7da9d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2165ac7da3d4a599fc428b39f3d6b1ad53d823add91fc6b8e7446e410fd3c8b7","slc_bf353cc592e9f520b0ae6a149180de30f3c4d22cdb17872ce8f7f37b972f9b0d","slc_c725ff51943399eb59ae7766f587872d7ba6d502a1fd21f6fb64d703ef783aa7"],"source_ids":["src_252cbbd8f1ef5a58b191a93308faeb03"],"text":"Plugins consist of paired Python and YAML files in a plugins folder (e.g. ascii_render.py and ascii_render.yaml) with required fields such as parameters and returns; sample plugins include anomaly_detection, ascii_render, klarna_search, and tell_joke.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
